		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φονο-άδαν</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>borne along, borne</i> or
				<i>carried in a litter</i> or the like , as a
			sick person, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Andr.</u>
				1166
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				888
			</span></i> (anap.), <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				42(1).122.27
			</span></i> (Epid., <span class="entity">iv B. C.</span>); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἦλθον οἴκαδε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					54.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἀνακομίζεσθαι, ἐκκομίζεσθαι,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				56.45
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>DMort.</u>
				14.5
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐν κλινιδίῳ φ. κομισθείς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Cor.</u>
					24
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>with rushing motion, violently,</i>
